# Dashboard-specific ignores.
#
# These live here rather than in the root .gitignore on purpose: the root
# file is owned by upstream (virattt/ai-hedge-fund), and this fork merges
# upstream on a schedule (.github/workflows/sync-upstream.yml). Every line
# added to an upstream-owned file is a merge conflict waiting to stop that
# sync, so fork-specific config stays in fork-specific files.

node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/
.env.local
next-env.d.ts

# Re-include this: the root .gitignore excludes *.txt, and requirements.txt
# is the Vercel function's dependency manifest. A negation in a nested
# .gitignore still wins for files (it would not for a directory).
!requirements.txt
